{#
    FR-066's removal confirmation.

    A page rather than a dialog, and the consequence is spelled out in the requirement's own
    terms before the button that causes it. The warning is placed *above* the confirm button and
    marked `role="alert"` so it is read before the control is reached, which is what the task's
    accessibility item asks for.

    Nothing here is destructive in the database sense: the association is deactivated and the
    history is kept (BR-066). The copy says so, because a parent who believes they have erased
    their child's record is being misled.
#}
{% extends 'family/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Remove {{ player.displayName }} from {{ trainerName }}{% endblock %}
{% block heading %}Remove {{ player.displayName }} from {{ trainerName }}?{% endblock %}

{% block family_content %}
    <div class="warning" role="alert">
        <p>
            This will cancel all upcoming RSVPs for {{ player.displayName }} with
            {{ trainerName }}, and {{ trainerName }} will no longer see them on their roster.
        </p>
        <p>
            Their attendance and history with {{ trainerName }} are kept, and you can add them
            back later.
        </p>
    </div>

    <form method="post" action="{{ path('family_trainer_remove', {id: player.id, organizationId: organizationId}) }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('submit') }}">
        <div class="actions">
            <button type="submit">
                <span aria-hidden="true">Remove</span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">Remove {{ player.displayName }} from {{ trainerName }}</span>
            </button>
            <a href="{{ path('family_index') }}">Keep them with {{ trainerName }}</a>
        </div>
    </form>
{% endblock %}
